---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial policy — Michael Rashkin" description="What I publish, evidence standards, opinion labeling, corrections, conflicts and sponsorships.">
  <section class="container" style="padding-top: 38px;">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>

      <h2>What I publish</h2>
      <p>
        I publish evidence-based analysis on nutrition, population health, and the social and policy forces that shape health outcomes.
        I also publish clearly labeled opinion when the evidence is incomplete or when values and tradeoffs matter.
      </p>

      <h2>Evidence standards</h2>
      <p>
        When I make a factual claim, I aim to cite primary sources, high-quality reviews, and clinical guidelines where applicable.
        When evidence is uncertain or mixed, I say so.
      </p>

      <h2>Opinion labeling</h2>
      <p>
        Opinion content is labeled. Interpretation is separated from factual claims.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If I discover an error, I correct it and record what changed on the Corrections page.
      </p>

      <h2>Conflicts and sponsorships</h2>
      <p>
        I disclose relevant financial relationships and conflicts on the Disclosures page.
      </p>

      <hr />
      <p class="muted small">
        Note: this page is static in the starter. You can move it into Sanity later if you want full CMS control.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
